---
title: Quick Collards With Bacon
source: direct-input
---

Add @bacon{7%slices} to a large #skillet{} and cook until crisp. Remove bacon from the pan, crumble, and set aside. Over medium heat, add @onion{1}(chopped) to the pan and cook until tender, about ~{5%minutes}. Add @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and cook until just fragrant. Add @collard greens{3%bunches}(picked, washed and cut) and fry until they start to wilt. Pour in @water{3%cups} and add @chicken bouillon{2%tbsp}, @pepper{1%tsp}, and @red pepper flakes{1%tsp}. Let simmer for ~{10%minutes}. Add @white vinegar{1%tbsp}, @brown sugar{1-2%tbsp}, and @hot sauce{}. Reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer for ~{45%minutes} or until greens are tender.